ce  and repay the loans they won't get them  they will go bust you have  non-performing assets  and that then leads to this downward  spiral where the banks then restrict  lending further  which pushes down asset prices further  which creates more bankruptcies more  non-performing loans this of course what  happened in japan  but it's also what happened um in in  many other  countries um in europe we had the same  situation in ireland portugal spain and  greece for instance  in the 2000s so the second one is when  banks  create credit for consumption  now that's the one that most people  think of money creation money printing  inflation turns out that's only one of  three fundamental scenarios  and you know when we had the so-called  great moderation in the us  um there was a massive expansion in the  money supply  but there was no inflation there was no  consumer price inflation why  well it was money creation bank credit  creation for  asset purchases it was the acid bubble  it wasn't really a moderation it's just  that's where you had your inflation acid  inflation  but it is true that when banks create  credit for consumption  you will get consumer price inflation  that's something we need to talk about  because 2020  2021 uh this is you know the mechanism  is now in place for that to become  uh quite prominent thirdly though  there's a third scenario and this is  really the  the redeeming feature of the banking  system and it is why the u.s  economy really if you look look back for  200 years has been one of the strongest  economies  in the world and why other countries  that have also been very successful in  the last  200 years like germany and then last 100  years japan last  50 years china they've done the same  namely the following  you ensure that the majority of your  bank  credit your money creation in the  banking system bank credit creation  is used not for asset purchases is used  not for consumption  but is used for business investment  that's the the golden rule of banking if  you ensure that  most of bank credit creation money  creation is used for business investment  in productive  investments that expand productivity  implement new technologies  increase goods and services create new  products that have value  of course there will always be failures  but overall it's a very of a different  kind from  asset purchases property and finance or  consumption  you know so as long as that's the  majority of your money creation  is actually for business investment and  of course  the biggest employer in all these  countries also the us  are small firms small firms are the most  important employer  it's around 70 percent of employment  in in the us in the uk and japan and  germany  germany japan actually it's close to 80  percent even  now these small firms they always credit  ration they don't need bank loans  they can't use you know the stock market  and and so on  so they need bank lending and if you  have bank lending for productive  purposes  ideally to small firms you will get  economic growth and no inflation  that's quite quite an extraordinary  insight because  we can have very high growth  and no inflation there's almost no limit  to economic growth  hang on some people say hang on aren't  there limits to growth didn't the club  of rome tell us  you know climate change and all that  we've got limits to growth  well not really actually there's a lot  of misunderstandings clearly we should  all  be careful to to treat the environment  well and things like pollution  and environmental degradation is bad but  growth as such is not the enemy because  what is growth growth can't be the enemy  because growth is an accounting fiction  it's just an accounting fiction there is  no economic growth you know ask a  physicist  you know tell me what's economic growth  how is the economy growing the  physicists will tell you no there's no  growth we know that the laws of  thermodynamics you know it's all the  same you're just transforming energy  from one state to another  but there's no growth that can't be  growth so we've created this accounting  fiction by  taking out certain statistical series  putting them together we call it gdp the  national income accounts  and that's what we're monitoring but gdp  as such is not  hurting the environment you know it's  not um  it is bad activities that can hurt the  environment we should avoid those that's  you know that's fine but it doesn't mean  we have to have zero growth or negative  growth  so we can have actually very high growth  the us has shown that in the past when  it was an emerging market and was  growing at  very high economic growth rates china  has shown this for 40 years double-digit  economic growth um is possible and  they did it by making sure bank credit  was guided essentially mainly for  productive business investment they  they stepped in they said no bank credit  for asset purchases and no bank credit  for consumption  of course recently you know the last 10  years they've liberalized that  but that's how you get very high growth

